                <pb facs="0953" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79620 Boeing Airplane Co./35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-09-28T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>64. Department’s 38, September 26, 3 p.m. Lawyer who holds O’Neil’s power of
                    attorney saw Director of Posts and Telegraphs this morning and was advised that
                    no contracts could be consummated in short time remaining of present
                    administration. He advised waiting till matter could be taken up with new
                    government. O’Neil’s lawyer counsels deferring further action until appointment
                    of new Director of Posts and Telegraphs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
